            <ArticleTitle>Neuralgic amyotrophy manifesting as anterior interosseous nerve palsy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>160-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neuralgic amyotrophy may present as a picture of anterior interosseous nerve palsy. In such a case, rather than a lesion of the nerve in the forearm, we offer indirect evidence of a lesion in the brachial plexus affecting discrete fiber bundles destined to form the anterior interosseous nerve.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
